    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Model call latency",
      "id": 16,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le, gen_ai_system) (rate(gen_ai_client_operation_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{gen_ai_system}}"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, gen_ai_system) (rate(gen_ai_client_operation_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{gen_ai_system}}"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, gen_ai_system) (rate(gen_ai_client_operation_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "C",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{gen_ai_system}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Wall-clock duration of ONE model call, bracketing the HTTP request only.\n\nIt deliberately excludes Activity scheduling. Folding Temporal queue latency in here would produce a panel labelled 'model latency' that rises when your OWN Worker fleet is backed up \u2014 blaming the provider for your capacity problem. To see that component, compare against activity schedule-to-start on the golden-signals board; the gap between them IS your queueing.\n\nBuckets run to 300s because a high-effort call on a hard prompt genuinely takes minutes. The OTel SDK's default boundaries stop at 10s, which would put every interesting call in +Inf and make every quantile here a lower bound rather than a measurement.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#199e70",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#ec835a",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "#d03b3b",
                "value": 60
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Model call errors by type",
      "id": 17,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 32
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (error_type, gen_ai_system) (rate(gen_ai_client_operation_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\", error_type!=\"\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 60",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{gen_ai_system}} \u00b7 {{error_type}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Failed model calls per minute, bucketed by a taxonomy chosen for WHAT YOU DO NEXT:\n\n  rate_limit    back off, or raise the account limit\n  overloaded    provider-side; retry, nothing to fix locally\n  auth          a human must rotate a key \u2014 retrying is pure waste\n  timeout       raise the Activity timeout, or lower effort\n  refusal       a content decision, NOT a fault; never retry the same prompt\n  bad_request   a malformed call, i.e. a code bug; also never retryable\n\nThe last three are marked NonRetryable in the Workflow's retry policy, so the same taxonomy drives both this panel and the retry decision. That is deliberate: a bucket added to one and not the other means paying three times for an error that was never going to succeed.\n\nerror_type is present ONLY on failures. Successful calls carry no such label, which is why this query filters on error_type!=\"\" rather than on a status value.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 25,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#199e70",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#d03b3b",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
