    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Unpriced models (spend is UNDER-REPORTED)",
      "id": 19,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (gen_ai_system, gen_ai_response_model) (rate(gen_ai_client_token_usage_sum{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\", gen_ai_token_type=\"output\"}[$__rate_interval])) unless sum by (gen_ai_system, gen_ai_response_model) (rate(gen_ai_client_cost_total{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\"}[$__rate_interval])) > 0",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Models that are burning output tokens but contributing NOTHING to the cost panels.\n\nThe pricing table is a hand-maintained list of published rates. A model missing from it contributes zero rather than a guess \u2014 a confident wrong number on a cost dashboard is worse than a visible gap, because someone will budget against it.\n\nThis panel is that visible gap. EMPTY IS THE HEALTHY STATE. Any row here means every cost figure on this board is an understatement, and the fix is to add the model's list price to agentPricing in demo/app/agent_types.go AND to PRICING in demo/agent-python/telemetry.py \u2014 both, or the two workers will disagree, which is what demo/agent-python/test_parity.py exists to catch.\n\nThe `unless` operator does the work: token series that have no matching cost series.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            }
          }
        },
