          "expr": "sum(rate(gen_ai_client_token_usage_sum{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\", gen_ai_token_type=\"input\"}[$__rate_interval])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(gen_ai_client_operation_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\", gen_ai_system=~\"$provider\", error_type=\"\"}[$__rate_interval])), 0.0001)",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "mean input tokens / call"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Mean input tokens per successful model call \u2014 a proxy for prompt size.\n\nIt is the leading indicator for the cost-per-run panel at the top, and it moves for reasons that are easy to ship without noticing: a system prompt that grew, a tool schema that got more verbose, retrieved context that stopped being truncated, or an agent taking more turns (each turn re-sends the entire conversation).\n\nA step change here immediately after a deploy is the cheapest cost regression you will ever catch, because the cause is in the diff.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "unit": "short",
